A little bird sang,

And when he paused I heard him say :
" Ah ! here's something I forgot to say;

To-morrow will not be as before ;
I am flying down to-day with sorrow and fear."

It's so sweet when mother gives me candy;
And, when she kisses my lips and caresses my hand,

I know what to do with it- I put it all away!

I am so glad to be back home again!

Oh what joy it brings—to have my mother and father here!

They are dearer than all the other folks that you see ;
For they gave their lives to save our loved ones from the foe;
And now we know by them—the meaning of Freedom’s high price.

Oh do not think we forget them while we live on this earth ;
While life endures may our hearts beat with freedom’s spirit there;

But when we lay down these mortal bodies as we sleep,
In honor let those

I loved you and it was so long,
 That I had to leave all my friends for thee;
 But I have found another love ;
 Who will be as dear to me as thou art !

The sea, when the wind is high, shall roll its breast;

And not before it is ready for the storm:

I am now at rest with my beloved friends!

"I saw them go by on their horses' backs, all silent;

But I knew that they had not seen me—
They were going to kill one another."
